speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, pursuant to Standing Order 43, I request unanimous consent of the House to move a motion dealing with an urgent matter, namely the proposed increase in power rates in the
Northwest Territories and Yukon. In view of the fact that these proposals are causing considerable debate among residents of the two territories; in view of the fact that this debate is severely limited by lack of adequate information about NCPC's operations; and in view of the fact that the government's only reaction to this widespread public concern has been to institute an in-house inquiry; I move, seconded by the hon. member for the Yukon (Mr. Nielsen);
That a full and public inquiry be conducted into the entire operation of the Northern Canada Power Commission in the Yukon and Northwest Territories under the supervision of either a supreme court judge or a public utilities board from one of the provinces. And further, that the findings of this inquiry be placed before the legislative assemblies of the two territories for approval, adoption or otherwise to ensure fullest possible public participation.
